From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 10:52:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS-Mythic: JIT-lock family (#74/#75/#80) + code-buffer
 lifetime hardening
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fork-only (upstream FEX bans AI-generated contributions).

threads holding FEX JIT locks. Dead-holder reaper + WritePriorityMutex grant
path + futex table + TEB slot-6 holder stamps.

through LatestMutex; pool-tail sweep remote-migrates generations pinned by
threads parked in wine waits (ml459 proved 13 live generations where steady
state needs ~2). MAX_CODE_SIZE capped at 32MB on iOS so every thread gets a
real buffer instead of a few hot threads exhausting the shared pool tail.

forever on InlineTail->SpinLockFutex — a lock word with no owner id, living in
the code buffer, not covered by any reaper; a holder that died or unwound while
its backpatch store faulted through the RX-alias emulator orphaned it. Now a
bounded acquire that stamps holder identity, and on timeout emulates the access
with the same helpers the non-JIT path uses, leaving the code unpatched.

Also: 128-bit CASPAL, EC-bitmap CompileBlock reverse-translate redirect (#52),
ThreadPauseHandler PauseReturnInstruction fix (#51), InvalidationTracker
exec-interval guard.

